WEBVTT

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:17.630
What is that thing?

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:20.620
Oh, it's something Mr. Giga
asked me to stick in the car.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.170
Here.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:26.070
Personal property, eh?

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.970
Why would a station bigshot make
production staff like us do this?

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:30.210
How should I know?

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:33.510
He said he'd have someone
come pick it up at the set later.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:36.510
Now step on it, or we'll have to
pay cabs to take the actors home.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:37.500
Yeah, yeah.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.750
What about tomorrow, Miss?

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.850
No, I'm okay, Mr. Kimura.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.920
The doctor said we can just
see how things go for a while.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:49.760
I'm glad to hear it.

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:08.340
Aw, look what's happened
to our precious Ryunka.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:11.610
That Geega is useless.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:16.020
But that one might make a good host.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:18.010
Maybe I'll try it out.

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:01.890
What the heck?!

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:04.060
Tuto, what's Geega's current location?

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:08.530
He's on Metropolitan Expressway
Route 6 heading towards Mukojima.

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:11.520
Fast! Too fast! What the hell?!

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:16.710
H-Hey! What's going on?! What's happening?!

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:19.140
Be quiet a minute!

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:20.710
I'll head there right away.

00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:23.250
Hurry. I can't get there fast enough.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:28.240
Honestly, pipe down! I'm going
to make you shut up for a while!

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:35.350
We're falling! We're falling! We're <i>falling!</i>

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:52.440
Where am I?

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:57.440
Where?

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:06.180
Why am I naked?

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:20.430
What the?

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:24.470
He's regained consciousness.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:28.080
Who are you?

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.310
Don't be afraid, Tsutomu Senkawa.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:33.280
H-How do you know my name?

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:35.420
And you, hurry up and wake up too.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:38.250
Huh? Me?

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:42.260
I am awake. I was just thinking
about how I should broach things.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:43.590
Huh?!

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:44.960
What was that?

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:49.170
Tsutomu Senkawa, I've learned
more or less who you are today, and...

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:51.130
Who are you?! Where are you?!

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:52.120
Hey!

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:56.270
What the heck is going on?!

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.740
Right now, I'm inside you.

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:03.180
Well, it'd be more accurate
to say that <i>you're</i> inside <i>me.</i>

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:04.310
What?!

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:06.680
Calm down. I'll explain it right now.

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:08.650
What <i>is</i> this?!

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:10.640
Keep watching the glass.

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:28.970
Huh?

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:33.140
Nice to meet you, Tsutomu. I'm Birdy Cephon.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:36.480
I'm an investigator with
the Space Federation Police.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.110
Shion Arita?

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:44.520
Oh, that's... um... my
"incognito persona," I guess?

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:46.490
I'm conducting an undercover
investigation here on Earth.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:48.960
I'm on the trail of some serious criminals.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:49.860
Huh?

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:53.900
Okay. I'll give it to you straight.

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:59.730
The truth is, yesterday, while I
was pursuing a criminal... I, uh...

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:06.510
What does that mean?

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:10.580
Basically, Tsutomu, you... um...

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:12.210
You died.

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:18.320
A b-b-bug!

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:21.190
You are currently what we'd call dead.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:25.030
Tsutomu Senkawa, I am Captain Megius

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:27.360
of the Space Federation
Police's Special Investigations Unit.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:29.500
As Birdy's superior,

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:32.030
I would like to offer you my
apologies and condolences.

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:32.900
Hold on...

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:34.570
But please don't worry.

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:38.010
Your body will be sent to a
medical lab at Econos-Quill,

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:40.410
where they will attempt to reconstruct it.

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:42.040
Hold on!

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:44.180
We'll be causing you some
inconvenience until that's complete,

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:48.250
but in the meantime Birdy will
provide her body as a substitute.

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:54.360
In other words, you can carry on
your life as Tsutomu Senkawa, as before.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:58.560
Now you just hang on a second!
You're not making any sense!

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:03.030
"Dead"? "Condolences"?
But I'm obviously still alive!

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:06.600
You can't believe what I'm telling you?

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:10.610
Forget what you're telling me;
I can't even believe a bug is talking.

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:14.880
See, it's because you freak out
like this that Geega got away from us.

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:17.580
I don't know anything about that!
What are you talking about?!

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.220
Like I said...

00:07:19.220 --> 00:07:23.410
We're falling! We're falling! We're <i>falling!</i>

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:30.590
I had the car brought around, Boss.

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:35.060
Ah, yes, my shiny new Beemer.

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:37.230
Where's my Beemer?

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:38.900
Boss! Boss!

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:42.270
Wait... Don't tell me?

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:43.900
My Beemer...

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:52.620
Tuto, where's Geega?

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:55.450
Unfortunately, I've lost him.

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:57.840
Damn!

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:00.350
Ugh!

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:06.000
What's with that?! You're saying it's <i>my</i> fault?!

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.630
Well, it <i>is!</i>

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:13.540
You tossed me onto the highway with
no warning! Like hell I could stay quiet!

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:15.340
Please, chase her out of my head!

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:17.470
I don't care if you're aliens or what,

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:21.380
but there's no way I want to
house some stranger inside me!

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:25.370
Tsutomu, you're laboring
under a misapprehension.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:34.690
Your body is...

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:39.500
Hey... what is this? If my
body is this messed up, I'll die!

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:42.130
Yes. To put it in simple terms,

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:45.200
we evacuated your
consciousness into Birdy's body.

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:49.640
Birdy's body is maintaining your life.

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:54.880
Birdy is not inside of you.
You are inside of Birdy.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:58.350
Until your body is restored,
your life force and consciousness

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:02.890
can only exist by temporarily
residing within Birdy.

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:04.220
This is a nightmare...

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:08.210
I can imagine how you must feel.
I'm sure you're tired, body and soul.

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:14.060
I don't even have the energy
to be shocked anymore.

00:09:14.060 --> 00:09:19.000
In that case, may I introduce myself?

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:22.740
My name is Tuto. I am Birdy's partner.

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:27.110
I feel some responsibility
for this incident as well.

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:32.680
If there's ever anything I can do,
please use Birdy to summon me.

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:34.080
Good night.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:45.390
It's a nightmare...

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:50.970
Don't be so depressed. I do feel bad about this.

00:09:50.970 --> 00:09:53.400
Hey. Tsutomu?

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:06.950
<i>This morning is just like any other.</i>

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:09.380
<i>The beginning of an ordinary day.</i>

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:15.220
<i>The sights I'm so used to</i>
<i>look too bright this morning...</i>

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:18.990
<i>...and they make my heart ache.</i>

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:29.170
<i>After all...</i>

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:35.140
...I'm dead.

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:37.980
I've apologized to you over and over!

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:41.180
The Earth phrase is "man up," right?

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:43.850
Man up and let it go already.

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:46.480
<i>You</i> get off your high horse!

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:54.000
More importantly, can't we talk
inside our heads, like telepathically?

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:57.970
If we do that, we might trigger mental fusion.

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:00.300
Practice whispering without moving your lips.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:02.340
I'm not a ventriloquist!

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:03.810
Hiya!

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:06.210
What are you doing mumbling to
yourself first thing in the morning?

00:11:06.210 --> 00:11:07.510
Hayamiya!

00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:09.280
You scared me!

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:13.620
What's up? You're in a bad mood already.
Did something happen?

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:15.220
Not really.

00:11:15.220 --> 00:11:17.210
Did you have another weird dream or something?

00:11:19.690 --> 00:11:26.560
Yeah, I guess you could say <i>I've</i>
become the ruined building now...

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:30.370
That cool-guy smirk
doesn't suit you. It's just creepy.

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:31.800
Hayamiya!

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:36.410
Morning, Kitamura. Something wrong?

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:38.970
You didn't hear about Nakasugi?

00:11:38.970 --> 00:11:41.010
What, did something happen to her?

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:43.000
She was in a car accident yesterday!

00:11:57.160 --> 00:12:01.360
Apparently she was on her way home
from the hospital she always goes to.

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:04.370
I hope she isn't hurt too badly...

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:08.540
Just go visit her. You guys are buds, right?

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:13.080
Plenty of time to get all
funeral-gloomy like this afterwards.

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:15.610
D-Don't say that, it's unlucky!

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:18.350
It's a time to mourn for the dead.

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:20.880
Yeah, we cremate the remains.

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:24.220
Oh, "cremate" is like "incinerate."

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:28.060
You know, burn to ashes...

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:29.760
U-Uh, I was just...

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:32.130
Senkawa! I can't believe you!

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:34.860
No, see, there's a good reason why l...

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:36.070
I just can't believe you!

00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:38.200
N-Now, now...

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:41.940
Anyway, let's all go visit her after school.

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:42.560
Okay?

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:50.580
Her consciousness still hasn't returned.
She's in critical condition.

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:56.580
We'll do everything we can, but you
may need to prepare for the worst.

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:04.130
Are you sure?

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:07.730
Absolutely. I've got the
best nose in the universe.

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:11.070
That was definitely the smell of an Altan.

00:13:11.070 --> 00:13:12.470
Which means the Ryunka is...

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:17.070
Yeah, that Birdy bitch must have taken it.

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:21.280
Damn it! We went to the trouble
of using people from this planet!

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:23.250
How did she figure it out?!

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:25.480
C'mon, cool down.

00:13:25.480 --> 00:13:28.020
They know your face now,
so you probably can't make a move.

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:30.920
I'll get it back for you.

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:33.320
They don't know what I look like yet,

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:36.310
and I don't care if she
<i>is</i> the Berserker Killer...

00:13:38.690 --> 00:13:41.760
So as payment, can I eat her?

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:46.170
I'm just so damn hungry!

00:13:46.940 --> 00:13:50.110
Yes, this is the Irma Agency.

00:13:50.110 --> 00:13:53.110
We appreciate your business, as always.

00:13:53.110 --> 00:13:56.710
Hmm? Shion Arita?

00:13:56.710 --> 00:14:00.150
Yes. That's fine.

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:02.850
Yes, that time slot is open.

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:07.720
Yes. A TV shoot? I'm afraid we can't...

00:14:07.720 --> 00:14:12.860
She'll be in stage makeup?
Oh, that should be all right, then.

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:18.300
5:00 pm at Yahata Studios, right.
Thank you in advance.

00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:22.030
Thank <i>you</i> in advance.

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:28.040
Oh, hi Ryo!

00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:29.030
Yo.

00:14:32.650 --> 00:14:33.750
You came.

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:36.220
She's a classmate.

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:40.690
Now, now, the more the
merrier for Nakasugi, right?

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:43.930
For that matter, isn't Senkawa late?

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:47.160
Honestly! I told him over
and over to be on time!

00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:53.690
"Yahata Studios"
"Authorized Personnel Only"

00:14:54.270 --> 00:14:57.770
Sheesh, you're late! Completely late!

00:14:57.770 --> 00:14:59.610
Sorry, Sir.

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:04.180
Now, Shion, punctuality is
the ironclad rule of this industry!

00:15:04.180 --> 00:15:05.510
Roger, yessiree.

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:06.950
Hey.

00:15:06.950 --> 00:15:08.380
What is it, Sir?

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:12.050
Cut the crap! What about the hospital visit?

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:15.260
I'm going with my friends to see Nakasugi!

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:16.560
What is it?

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:21.260
Tsutomu's miffed about the
sudden change in plans, yessiree.

00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:24.930
Oh, that's show biz!
That's what it is to be talent!

00:15:24.930 --> 00:15:27.740
It's hard to survive in this business!

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:30.140
Come on, let's go.

00:15:30.140 --> 00:15:33.130
Why do you guys even <i>want</i> to survive in it?!

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:34.900
"Echigoya"

00:15:37.110 --> 00:15:39.550
What is it, young lady?

00:15:39.550 --> 00:15:41.880
I-It's my chronic condition...

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:45.950
"Oh no!" says the nice man, trying to help her.

00:15:45.950 --> 00:15:49.290
Then the bad guys beat him up
and kidnap the merchant's daughter.

00:15:49.290 --> 00:15:51.730
This is your only scene, but...

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:57.930
Everyone's late, huh Sir?

00:15:57.930 --> 00:16:02.070
Yes, it's odd. I thought the filming
was supposed to start at 5:00...

00:16:02.070 --> 00:16:03.270
Tuto!

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:05.940
Watch out, Birdy. It's a blaster.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:10.140
Oh, my, did I miss?

00:16:12.510 --> 00:16:14.350
Who are you?

00:16:20.920 --> 00:16:23.930
How about you give the Ryunka back?

00:16:23.930 --> 00:16:28.200
Or shall I gobble you up?
It'll only hurt for a second!

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:29.160
Bacillus!

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:32.600
Don't call me by that name!

00:16:40.780 --> 00:16:46.650
What are you and Geega plotting, Bacillus?

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:50.850
Did you alter your body so much
you screwed up your memories, too?

00:16:50.850 --> 00:16:52.720
<i>You're</i> the one who'll hand over the Ryunka!

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:55.860
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:57.060
Who is that guy?!

00:16:57.060 --> 00:17:02.230
He's Bacillus, a serious
offender wanted by the Federation.

00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:04.330
He lives parasitically on other organisms.

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:07.870
When he takes them over, he takes
in their memories and knowledge, too.

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:09.670
Is he an alien too?

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:15.040
Yes. But that body is an Earthling's.
He must have taken it.

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:19.650
This is a pain... Shall I eat you?

00:17:19.650 --> 00:17:26.050
That's right! If I do that,
I'll know where the Ryunka is, too!

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:33.900
Gross!

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:37.520
What are you doing, Birdy?
Hurry up and get away from him.

00:17:38.900 --> 00:17:40.070
I'll eat you!

00:17:40.070 --> 00:17:41.200
He's coming! He's coming!

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:41.870
Birdy.

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:43.860
Like hell you will!

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:48.230
I'll eat you!

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:26.720
Amazing...

00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:30.550
Isn't that woman Shion Arita after all?

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:35.320
Man, am I sick?

00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:37.130
Hey, are you okay?!

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:38.890
Be quiet!

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:40.890
That investigator... is a hard pill to swallow!

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:53.330
It's no good...

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:57.410
I gotta get out of here.

00:18:57.410 --> 00:18:59.400
There you are!

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:02.980
There's no mistake this time.

00:19:09.490 --> 00:19:10.920
Oh, crap!

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:20.320
Birdy! There's a man...
A man collapsed down there!

00:19:23.670 --> 00:19:27.310
I'll be back, in a new body.

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:30.350
- I won't let you escape!
- Are you going to kill again?!

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:32.970
You're going to let someone else die, like me?

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:41.390
It's okay. He's just passed out.

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:45.690
Hey, it's Mr. Muroto.

00:19:45.690 --> 00:19:46.680
Uh-oh!

00:19:50.170 --> 00:19:52.170
You know him?

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:55.240
Keisuke Muroto. He graduated from my school.

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:57.170
He calls himself a journalist.

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:59.370
He's fishy...

00:19:59.370 --> 00:20:02.740
Birdy, someone's coming. Let's withdraw.

00:20:02.740 --> 00:20:03.730
Okay.

00:20:05.310 --> 00:20:09.580
You moron! And you had
the gall to come back here?!

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:11.420
Sorry, Boss.

00:20:11.420 --> 00:20:14.720
Dammit, I gotta do something fast.

00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:18.990
If Shyamalan or Gomez finds
out I don't have the Ryunka...

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:20.660
What?

00:20:20.660 --> 00:20:26.330
Boss... This body's at its limit!

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:29.270
I'm so hungry... I'm so hungry!

00:20:29.270 --> 00:20:32.500
H-H-Hold on! Hey!

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:39.410
Senkawa!

00:20:39.410 --> 00:20:40.550
Hayamiya...

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:44.250
I can't believe you didn't come yesterday!
What were you thinking?!

00:20:44.250 --> 00:20:48.390
You wouldn't answer your phone, either!
I didn't know you were so heartless!

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:51.760
No, see, I had my reasons...

00:20:51.760 --> 00:20:55.630
Oh, hey, what about Nakasugi? How was she?

00:20:55.630 --> 00:20:57.460
Well, she...

00:20:59.630 --> 00:21:02.370
Nakasugi!

00:21:02.370 --> 00:21:04.810
Morning, Hayamiya.

00:21:04.810 --> 00:21:07.880
Thanks for coming to visit me yesterday.

00:21:07.880 --> 00:21:09.610
Are you really okay?

00:21:09.610 --> 00:21:10.650
Yup, I'm fine.

00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:12.580
Seriously, you're really lucky!

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:16.050
So, that's great, huh?
Seems like it wasn't anything serious.

00:21:16.050 --> 00:21:17.450
Don't you talk about it.

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:21.320
Don't be so mad. We're going to
be together for a while, anyway.

00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:23.990
Like you Earthlings say,

00:21:23.990 --> 00:21:29.100
we're like, uh, two peanuts...
two chestnuts... What is it, again?

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:30.600
Like cats and dogs.

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:34.800
Yeah! Exactly! Let's get along, okay?

00:21:34.800 --> 00:21:36.240
Give me a break.

